       47  '''Anenii Noi District''' ({{langx|ro|Raionul Anenii Noi}}, {{IPAc-ro|pron|a|'|n|e|n|ii|_|'|n|oi}}) is a district (''[[Administrative divisions of Moldova|raion]]'') in the central part of [[Moldova]]. As of 2024, its population was 57,687. Its seat is the city of [[Anenii Noi]].
       48  ==History==
       49  Localities with the oldest documentary attestation are [[Gura Bîcului]], [[Teliţa]], [[Mereni, Anenii Noi|Mereni]] documented for the first time in 1443–1475. The following [[centuries]] shows development in the economy (trade, agriculture, customs duties), and a significant demographic growth. The 
       50  ==Geography==
       51  [[File:Castel Mimi vedere generală.jpg|thumb|General view of Mimi Castle.]]
       52  Anenii Noi District is located in the central part of Moldova. Neighborhood has the following district: [[Criuleni District]] in north, east [[Grigoriopol sub-district|Grigoriopol District]], [[Căuşeni District]] in south, [[Ialoveni District]] and [[Chişinău|Municipality of Chişinău]] in the west. 
       53  ===Climate===
       54  Temperate [[continental climate]] with annual average temperature {{convert|10|C|0}}, July average temperature {{convert|22|C|0}}, January average temperature {{convert|-4|C|0}}. Yearly precipitation 500–600 mm. Average wind speed 3–5 m\s.
       55  ===Fauna===
       56  Fauna typical of central Europe this mammals such as [[fox]]es, [[hedgehog]]s, [[deer]], [[wild boar]], [[Stoat|ermine]], [[ferret]] and more. Of birds: [[owl]], [[stork]], [[hawk]], [[Old World sparrow|sparrow]], [[starling]], [[crow]], [[egret]], [[partridge]]s and others.
       57  ===Flora===
       58  Forests occupy 10.7% of the district and are complemented by [[oak]], [[english oak]], [[hornbeam]], [[maple]], [[Silver Linden|linden]], [[Ash (Fraxinus)|ash]] and others. From plants: [[Artemisia (plant)|wormwood]], [[black]], [[clover]], [[knotweed]], [[Urtica|nettle]], [[fescue]] and more.
       59  ===Rivers===
       60  Anenii Noi District is located in the [[Nistru]] river basin, which crosses the district in the east. The most important tributary of this is [[Bîc River]] (155 km). The largest lake is Lake Sălaș located near locality [[Gura Bîcului]], with an area of {{cvt|3.72|km2}}. It is the third largest natur
       61  ==Administrative subdivisions==
       62  Anenii Noi District has 1 town, 25 communes and 19 villages.
